Inert-edit probe — FILED EVIDENCE, not a re-runnable gate.
==========================================================

Run 2026-09-16 on `platterpus-fork` at d92c4e1, in a detached git worktree so
this tree was never dirty.

WHAT IT ANSWERS. `tools/mutate.py` reports a mutation score, and that score is
vacuous if any test in the suite detects the EDIT rather than the DEFECT --
such a test kills every mutant and the sweep reports 100%. `EXCLUDED_TESTS`
names the ones that do. The list is derived-and-named rather than pattern
filtered, so it cannot grow by itself, and mutate.py's own docstring says the
probe "is worth repeating rather than trusting this comment". This is that
repeat.

It had not been repeated since three tests were added to the images suite:
`cache_table_matches_the_transcripts`, `encode_failure_is_absent_from_the_log`,
and check 2b inside `docs_do_not_contradict_themselves`. All three appear below
as OK, so none of them detects an edit.

THE EDIT. Three lines appended at EOF of `src/utils.c`, moving no line number:

    /* Behaviourally inert probe edit: a comment at EOF, moving no line number.
     * Appended to ask which tests detect an EDIT rather than a DEFECT. */

Confirmed landed before the run: `git diff --stat` reported `src/utils.c | 3
+++`, and the build was green (ninja regenerated version.c and
handshake_state.h and linked without error) -- a probe whose edit did not
compile would run the stale binary and report a clean sweep for the wrong
reason.

THE RESULT. 84 OK, 1 FAIL. The one failure is `images - cyanrip:contract_build`,
which is exactly what `EXCLUDED_TESTS` names and the only entry it has.
**The exclusion list is still complete.**

SECOND FINDING, not what the probe was for. `cyanrip:Sanitizer sweep` PASSED.
That is the other edit-detector CLAUDE.md records: `tools/sanitize-run.py` used
to run the whole images suite including `contract_build`, so mutants died on the
edit through the sweep and `src/cyanrip_encode.c` scored 100.0% over 125
mutants and meant nothing. Under an inert edit that sweep would fail if it still
carried `contract_build`. It does not.

RE-RUN IT DELIBERATELY, not on a schedule -- it is a full build plus the whole
85-test suite, about seven minutes:

    git worktree add --detach <tmp> HEAD
    printf '\n/* inert */\n' >> <tmp>/src/utils.c
    cd <tmp> && meson setup build && ninja -C build && meson test -C build
    # expect: exactly the tests EXCLUDED_TESTS names, and no others, FAIL

